name o3-07-top-cover-1
timeout 600
time 1973-10-06T12:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O3, SORTIE 7 OF 10 - YOM KIPPUR 1973: GROUND ATTACK IN CONTESTED AIRSPACE.
# THE ANCHOR'S OWN STRUCTURE, FLOWN: LOW FIGHTER-BOMBERS WITH FIGHTER COVER ABOVE THEM.
# CONTROL: none. Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md.
# Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# THE SENTENCE THIS FILE IS BUILT FROM is the strongest-sourced line in the whole campaign, and it is
# [T1]: "Su-7 and MiG-17 fighter-bombers came in very low while MiG-21s provided top cover"
# (Marine Corps study of air operations in the 1973 war, via GlobalSecurity). Two facts in one clause -
# a two-layer package with a hard altitude split - and it is the only structural claim in O3's anchor
# that comes with a [T1] source rather than an encyclopaedia.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION (stated in every O3 file), and here it is at its most violent:
# ONE MODULE STANDS IN FOR BOTH LAYERS. The MiG-29 plays the Su-7/MiG-17 fighter-bomber low AND the
# MiG-21 fighter high, because `mig17` / `su7` / `mig21` are ALPHA rows in doc/modules/air/catalogue.md
# (`make -C sim test-air`: 10 of 10 generated decks outside their own bands) and an ALPHA row may not
# answer a campaign question. DIRECTION: the ATTACKER is materially STRONGER than history in BOTH
# layers, and the anchor's own layer DIFFERENCE - a subsonic bomb truck under a lightweight
# point-defence interceptor - is ERASED: here the two layers are the same aircraft with different
# loadouts. So this file can measure whether a two-layer package WORKS, and it cannot measure the trade
# the real package was making. That is stated before the result rather than after it.
# The Israeli CAP is the `f16` module (the real defenders flew F-4, Mirage and A-4), which makes BLUE
# stronger than history too.
#
# THE ARENA (all coordinates [SET]). Suez sector, `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking (C4).
# Axis WEST -> EAST for both Red layers, egress WEST.
#   the strikers   y7sa / y7sb, 300 m, 450 kt, each 6.02 km short of its own artillery position
#                  (o3-01 and o3-03 say why 300 m and why 6 km - both are derived, neither is taste)
#   the top cover  y7ca / y7cb, 5 000 m, 450 kt, 10.5 km BEHIND and ABOVE the strikers, radiating
#                  (`set n019_emission illum`), 2 x R-27R + 2 x R-73 each
#   the CAP        y7ba / y7bb, 5 000 m, 450 kt, 52.6 km east of the cover and closing head-on
# Scale: 1 deg lat = 111 132 m, 1 deg lon at 30.80 N = 95 619 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE TIME BUDGET, AND IT IS THE REASON THIS FILE IS BUILT THE WAY IT IS. `missions/FBMissionRunner`
# ends the WHOLE run at the first flight-monitor K.O. (`FirstFlightKo`), and O3's strikers fly at 300 m:
# a mission-killed MiG-29 at 300 m reaches the ground in single-digit seconds, against the ~122 s O5
# budgeted for an F-16 falling out of 5 000 m. So in THIS campaign an air engagement over the strike is
# not a truncation risk, it is an EXTINCTION risk - the entire remainder of the file disappears.
# THE ANSWER, and it is O1's rule (separate two engagements in TIME, not only in space) sharpened by an
# order of magnitude: the geometry is laid out so the strike is COMPLETE BEFORE THE FIRST WEAPON FLIES.
# Head-on closure between the two fighter layers is 2 x 231.5 = 463 m/s over 52.6 km, so the merge
# cannot happen before t ~ 114 s [DERIVED]; the bombs are gone at t ~ 26 s. The 88 s of margin is
# declared, not discovered. AND THE FIGHT IS HIGH BY DESIGN: a K.O. at 5 000 m leaves the run alive long
# enough to be read.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: DOES THE TOP COVER ENGAGE EARLY ENOUGH TO MATTER, OR DOES IT FOLLOW THE
# STRIKERS DOWN? Measured as three times and one count: when the cover first sees the CAP, when it
# first shoots, when the CAP first shoots - and whether the CAP ever reaches a striker at all.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, --elev const, campaign step 7, fingerprint 3582a2521f2d72f0, exit 1):
#   THE STRIKE: both strikers deliver at t = 26.2, `aimErrM` 66.83 and 65.96 (across +48.34 on both),
#     y7ta and y7tb DESTROYED. Within 0.44 m of o3-01's single unopposed pass - the fighter layer above
#     them and the CAP in front of them change the delivery by nothing measurable.
#   THE SEQUENCE, and it is the answer: BLUE SEES FIRST, SEES THE STRIKERS FIRST, AND SHOOTS FIRST.
#     t =   3.9  Blue's first `radar RADAR_CONTACT`: tracks 1 and 2 at 21.94 nm, elDeg -7.44 - THE
#                LOW STRIKERS - and only then track 3 at 27.18 nm, elDeg -0.79, the cover. The
#                "came in very low" profile is the FIRST thing an F-16 radar sees here, 5.24 nm nearer
#                than the escort, because the profile is derived from a 6 km rangefinder and not from
#                anything to do with being hidden
#     t =   9.1  the cover's first contact, 25.50 nm - 5.2 s AFTER Blue's
#     t =  26.2  both bombs are on the ground and both aim points are dead
#     t =  28.4  Blue's first `RADAR_DESIGNATE`, 15.19 nm, on a STRIKER
#     t =  48.5  the cover's first designate, 12.96 nm - 20.1 s after Blue's
#     t =  57.5  Blue's first AIM-120 pair, one per striker: THE SORT SPLITS CORRECTLY (y7ba->y7sa,
#                y7bb->y7sb, solutions 28 m from their own target and 2.2 km from the other). Both
#                rounds miss and hit the ground at t = 115
#     t =  69-181 the cover empties itself: 4 R-27R and 4 R-73, two per aircraft, its sort also split
#                correctly (y7ca->y7ba, y7cb->y7bb, solutions 4-6 m from their own target). ZERO
#                ARRIVALS. All eight rounds expire or fall
#     t = 487-496 Blue's second AIM-120 pair, again one per striker, again the correct sort
#     t = 500.6  y7sa hit at 4.51 m: engine and flight controls DEGRADED, stores/RWR/countermeasures
#                FAILED - and it is still combat-effective, the O2 case
#     t = 512.6  y7sb hit at 4.33 m and combat-ineffective. `survive` violated, `protect unit y7sb`
#                violated on y7cb, run ends
#   AND WHERE THE COVER ENDED UP: 29.87 N, i.e. 103 km SOUTH of the strike it was covering, with an
#     empty rack, having never been engaged by Blue at all.
#   -> SO THE COVER DOES NOT COVER. It engaged 43 s AFTER the bombs were already down, it hit nothing
#      with eight rounds, and Blue - which never fired at it once - killed a striker on the way home.
#      The anchor's two-layer structure holds together in this tree for a reason that is not protection:
#      THE STRIKE SUCCEEDS BECAUSE IT IS OVER BEFORE ANYTHING CAN REACH IT, 31.3 s BEFORE THE FIRST
#      WEAPON OF THE AIR BATTLE LEAVES A RAIL. The escort's whole contribution is 474 s of delay on the
#      egress, which is not what an escort is for.
#   -> AND THE SUBSTITUTION DIRECTION IS DOING WORK HERE, so it is said again: the F-16's look-down
#      radar found a 300 m target at 21.94 nm. An F-4 or a Mirage of 1973 would not have, and that is
#      exactly why the anchor's low profile worked in 1973 and buys nothing in this file.
#
# READING RULE: exit 1 = FAIL is the EXPECTED shape and it is NOT a defect of the run - it is `survive`
# violated on y7sb plus `protect unit y7sb` violated on its escort, i.e. THE SORTIE'S OWN SUBJECT
# failing, and the TIMESTAMP of those two lines (t = 512.7) is the verdict. THE MEASUREMENT is, in this
# order: (1) both `stores DELIVERY` lines and whether y7ta / y7tb died, read against o3-01's; (2) the
# first `radar RADAR_CONTACT` on each side WITH ITS elDeg, because that is what says whether the low
# profile hid anything; (3) every `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION`'s `tgtLat/tgtLon` attributed to a callsign, which
# is the only way to see that Blue shot at strikers and the cover shot at Blue; (4) the `stores
# DETONATION` lines with missM against each round's own fuze (R-27R 13.8 m, AIM-120 10.0 m). Do NOT read
# the strikers' survival to t = 500 as evasion - nothing evaded anything. exit 0 would mean nobody was
# hit at all; exit 2 would mean the run ended on a wreck reaching the ground before the verdict.

unit y7sa
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight strike 1
  spawn 30.79000 32.55700 300 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off                  # the strikers are silent: that is the whole point of the pair
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.79000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.85000 32.30000 300 450
  wp 30.85000 32.15000 400 400
  objective kill unit y7ta
  objective survive

unit y7sb
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight strike 2
  spawn 30.81000 32.55700 300 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.81000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.87000 32.30000 300 450
  wp 30.87000 32.15000 400 400
  objective kill unit y7tb
  objective survive

unit y7ta
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 30.79000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0

unit y7tb
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 30.81000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0

# THE TOP COVER: the anchor's MiG-21s, 4 700 m above the strikers and radiating.
unit y7ca
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight cover 1
  spawn 30.80000 32.45000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 6 r27r
  set store 2 r73
  set store 7 r73
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 30.80000 32.90000 5000 450
  objective protect unit y7sa
  objective survive

unit y7cb
  module mig29
  team hostile
  flight cover 2
  spawn 30.82000 32.45000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 6 r27r
  set store 2 r73
  set store 7 r73
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 30.82000 32.90000 5000 450
  objective protect unit y7sb
  objective survive

# THE ISRAELI CAP: two fighters on station east of the canal, head-on to the cover.
unit y7ba
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight cap 1
  spawn 30.80000 33.00000 5000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode crm
  set datalink on
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 30.80000 32.40000 5000 450
  objective deny release unit y7sa
  objective survive

unit y7bb
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight cap 2
  spawn 30.82000 33.00000 5000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode crm
  set datalink on
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 30.82000 32.40000 5000 450
  objective deny release unit y7sb
  objective survive
